title The reading a run publishes about the worth it weighed, read once for the whole ladder
prompt Kyri, read the canon and the card, hold Standfast, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, and send it.
think Standfast opened the lap and ran clear. The REDS ledger witness lives at tools/gen/season/reds_ledger_monotone_witness.rish rather than tools/, which cost one FileNotFound before the roster in glow_tend_era_suite.rish named its real path -- measurement beats memory, including memory of where a tool sits. It prints measured=128, headline_total=128, disagreements=0, verdict=ok, so every living row stands closed and no red books the allocation.
think The running thread came off the top three rows of the log index and the newest recommend line, and the carry witness's own printed queue agreed with them. Three independent records named appraisal_published as the head that widens nothing, so the head was taken on agreement rather than on any one of them being trusted.
think The family was verified before it was folded. Hashing the body of appraisal_published across the 110 caravan modules returned one hash thirty-eight times at twenty lines apiece, so no rung carries its own variant -- unlike the deem, owe, avow, and meet rungs of earlier laps, where the rung's own subject was the family's subject. Then all five symbols the body reaches -- max_queue_len, max_note_path_len, note_path, plan_name, phase_bit -- were checked for a leading pub in every one of the thirty-eight, and all five were already public everywhere.
think The lift moved the twenty-line body into caravan/ladder_checks.rye as pub fn appraisal_published(comptime rung: type, io: std.Io, held: u32) u32, qualifying each of the five reached symbols through the type parameter, and replaced each rung's body with a three-line stub returning ladder_checks.appraisal_published(@This(), io, held). Every rung already imports the harness, so no import line moved anywhere.
obs Prediction met measurement to the digit for the eighth lap running. The realized fall is (identical_copies - 1) x (body_lines - stub_lines) and a stub is the signature plus two lines, so 37 x (20 - 3) = 629. Carry fell 76,971 to 76,342 -- a fall of 629. Delegates rose 2,803 to 2,841, exactly the thirty-eight stubs, which is how a reader tells a fold from a cost moved somewhere cheaper to count. Bodies 18,161 to 18,162 and distinct 7,957 to 7,958 -- the one published body the fold added. Families hold at 705.
obs Lindy-first chose 629 over 720 for the fourth lap running, and the reason keeps holding. renew_path returns about 720 and ask_path about 660, and both stand private in all thirty-one rungs, so either would open a seam across thirty-one declarations before it paid. A fall taken without widening stays cheap on the long return.
obs The next head is measured rather than inherited. recant_published hashes one body thirty-seven times at twenty lines and declares pub in all thirty-seven, with the same five reached symbols public throughout, so it returns 612 and widens nothing. Lifting it closes the glyph-note family: bearing_published, lost_published, appraisal_published, and recant_published each open a glyph note, walk it against the held count, and fold it to a phase mask, differing only in the note suffix and the glyph. After that a single body taking suffix and glyph as comptime parameters becomes one readable round.
obs Council rota, row zero -- Aether and Jupiter, why the work exists. The compass named the read order and its own amendment to Lindy-first crux-first, which is the order this lap took. The Lindy effect priced the choice directly: a fold that widens nothing keeps the seam narrow for the reader who arrives three years on, and a fall of 629 taken without opening thirty-one declarations is the more durable bet than a fall of 720 that opens them. The grain and the crossing held the register honest -- sameness as compression counts the whole cost of a line saved, and the stub count is exactly that accounting written where a reader can check it.
